# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
mutants/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Node
node_modules/

# Review agent: cloned beside the project, and its per-run evidence.
# The evidence is worth keeping on disk and out of history.
multi-model-code-review-agent/
data/reviews/
audit.json
gate-output.txt

# Card data downloaded from Scryfall; regenerated by `mtgcoach sets add`.
data/cache/
data/*.sqlite3

# The server's bearer tokens, one per seat. Made on first run, per
# installation, and the whole of the access control -- see
# services/api/src/mtgcoach/api/seating.py.
data/token

# Self-play journals: one line per coach decision, holding the full briefing,
# so a season runs to megabytes. The command that made each one is in
# docs/SELFPLAY.md, which is what makes them reproducible without keeping them.
data/selfplay/

# Downloaded card data. Four megabytes of Scryfall's JSON per set, and it is
# theirs rather than ours -- `mtgcoach sets fetch` puts it back.
data/scryfall/

# The Comprehensive Rules. Wizards' document, revised with every set, and not
# ours to redistribute -- the operator installs it and CI fetches its own copy.
# Which revision a game or a check used is recorded rather than vendored; see
# packages/rules/src/mtgcoach/rules/effective.py.
data/rules/

# Unreviewed extractor output. Only the sealed fixture and its manifest are
# data; `mtgcoach effects seal` is the only way across that line.
data/sets/*/proposals.json

# The app's dependencies. `npm install` in apps/mobile restores them.
apps/*/node_modules/
apps/*/.expo/
apps/*/dist/

# Claude Code's own per-session state. Machine- and process-specific: a lock
# naming one laptop's pid is meaningless anywhere else, and it arrived here by
# being written into the working tree while a commit was being made.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json
